  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Prove that for all $n\\ge1$\n$$\\frac{1}{1^2}+\\frac{1}{2^2}+\\frac{1}{3^2}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{n^2}\\le2-\\frac1n.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "True for all integers $n\\ge1$.\n\nUse the inductive bound and $\\frac1k-\\frac1{k+1}-\\frac1{(k+1)^2}=\\frac1{k(k+1)^2}>0$.",
      "worked": "Let $S_n=\\frac1{1^2}+\\frac1{2^2}+\\cdots+\\frac1{n^2}$.\n\nBase case: $S_1=1=2-\\frac11$.\n\nInductive hypothesis: assume $S_k\\le2-\\frac1k$, where $k\\ge1$.\n\nFor the required comparison,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1k-\\frac1{k+1}-\\frac1{(k+1)^2}&=\\frac{(k+1)^2-k(k+1)-k}{k(k+1)^2}\\\\\\frac1k-\\frac1{k+1}-\\frac1{(k+1)^2}&=\\frac1{k(k+1)^2}\\\\\\frac1k-\\frac1{k+1}-\\frac1{(k+1)^2}&>0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $-\\frac1k+\\frac1{(k+1)^2}<-\\frac1{k+1}$.\n\nInductive step:\n$$\\begin{align*}S_{k+1}&=S_k+\\frac1{(k+1)^2}\\\\S_{k+1}&\\le2-\\frac1k+\\frac1{(k+1)^2}\\\\S_{k+1}&<2-\\frac1{k+1}.\\end{align*}$$\nIn particular, $S_{k+1}\\le2-\\frac1{k+1}$. Therefore, by mathematical induction, the result holds for all integers $n\\ge1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 128
  },
